{
  "requirement": "The Rust caller receives the node's complete `D::NodeContent` or the domain's read error.\n\nThe tool reads a known node, such as the current node or a target from `outgoing_edges`.\nEach page’s `text` contains the next portion of the node’s formatted contents. Formatting follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the marked tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.read_node.behavior`. I did not read any implementation source. The judgment rests on the supplied test text.\n\n**Rust caller gets the complete `D::NodeContent` or the domain's read error**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` runs two inputs. One is empty. The other is a long multi-byte string of about 16k \"é\" and \"終\" characters followed by \"end\".\n- It asserts that `read_snapshot` and `read` return contents whose `format()` equals the original.\n- It asserts that a returned value keeps its contents after the graph changes.\n- It asserts that `read(&9)` returns the domain error `\"missing\"` and records no dependency.\n- `fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` also checks that read errors from `read(&2)` are returned.\n\n**The tool reads a known node: the current node, or a target from `outgoing_edges`**\n- `fn[a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation]`, `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` and `fn[graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change]` call `read_node` on the current node, Node 1.\n- `fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` calls `outgoing_edges` on Node 1. It then calls `read_node` on the returned target, Node 2, and checks that the delivered contents were recorded as a `Dependency::Node`.\n\n**Each page's `text` holds the next portion of the formatted contents**\n- `fn[a_complete_node_read_has_text_and_no_continuation]` asserts that a short node returns exactly `{\"text\":\"short text\"}` with no continuation.\n- `fn[graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change]` uses a multi-byte string long enough to need two pages. It follows `get_next_page` and asserts a `next` entry on the first page only. It asserts that the concatenated page `text` equals the original, even though the underlying contents change between calls.\n- `fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` pages through an 18,000-character node and checks the recorded fingerprint holds the full value.\n- `fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]` checks that concurrent paged reads keep their own pages.\n\n**Formatting follows the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`**\n- The paging and short-read tests compare tool output with the formatted contents.\n- `fn[node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents]` makes the formatter or preparation fail. It asserts that the agent receives an `is_error` tool result named `read_node` with the error message. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and that the agent can continue and submit a result. This covers the cited requirement's rule that failures during a `read_node` call become tool errors.\n- `fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]` uses a custom formatter, `distinct_pages`.\n\nI found no obligation or named boundary case that lacks a test with a relevant assertion.",
